"},{"text":"T","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"QueryTerm","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryTerm","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule9QueryTermP","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"query","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The query whose matches to watch.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"hook","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The closure to run, given the world and the entity that started matching."}]}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use this method to respond when an entity gains the combination of components a query","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"describes, rather than a single component. The hook runs when spawning, inserting,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"removing or applying a command makes an entity match. Entities that already match when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you register the hook don’t run it. Query hooks run at the same point component hooks do","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(see the component ","type":"text"},{"code":"onAdd(_:perform:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only the query’s structural conditions count: its component terms and the types its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"filter requires, excludes or skips by default, the conditions a cache of the query keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/cache(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). The following example counts the entities that start moving:"}]},{"code":["struct MoverCount: Resource { var count = 0 }","","